    "sha": "a8355fa8ce92c0083bf387f846ac71d71d749d11",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKGE4MzU1ZmE4Y2U5MmMwMDgzYmYzODdmODQ2YWM3MWQ3MWQ3NDlkMTE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T09:46:18Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T09:46:18Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(sim,app): turning programs simulate on the field eye about their fitted spindle, with meridian parity\n\nplan_program no longer refuses the Turn family. The plan carries the\ninsert's nose radius and the op's fitted lathe axis (re-fitted with\nturning::profile::Frame::about from operation::source_facets - the\ngenerator's own material read), and the field eye (stock_view,\nstock_play) cuts each lathe op through the revolved nose stadium about\nthat axis (Stock::simulate_lathe_about, new LatheAxis in\nstock_sim::field_lathe; simulate_lathe keeps world +Z). A chord's\nsecond end is now signed against the first's side, so a parting chord\npast centre is the meridian segment it is.\n\nGrooving/parting blades, threading inserts and form gauges refuse by\nname (LATHE_BLADE_REFUSAL, the blade-profile sweep is #21). The column\nverdict (simulate_document) refuses any lathe program by name\n(LATHE_VERDICT_REFUSAL), so the post gate still shows \"not judged\".\nA lathe op's plan radius is its nose (the display cell law).\n\nReadings (debug, 0.5 mm cell, sign at every cell centre two cells\ninside the stock against the meridian law written in the test):\nfacing 438,976 centres / 10,680 cut / 0 misses; facing about an\noff-origin axis (3, -2) 0 misses; profile rough+finish 438,976 /\n11,992 / 0; multi-pass contour 438,976 / 9,160 / 0; boring 429,777 /\n2,904 / 0.\n\nPinned by: lathe_field_sim (facing_simulates_on_the_field_with_\nmeridian_parity, a_bar_off_the_origin_is_turned_about_its_own_fitted_\naxis, profile_rough_and_finish_simulate_with_meridian_parity,\nmulti_pass_contour_simulates_with_meridian_parity, boring_simulates_\ninside_the_bore_with_meridian_parity, a_grooving_blade_is_refused_by_\nname_and_the_verdict_refuses_the_lathe); stock_lathe::a_stated_axis_\noff_the_origin_cuts_the_same_meridian.\n\nFixes #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
