      "message": "fix(sim,app): a lathe chord skewed off one meridian refuses by name; review fixes for the field lathe sim\n\n- LatheSweep::of is fallible: a chord whose ends stand in different\n  planes through the axis (a hyperboloid sweep the flat meridian\n  segment under-claims) refuses by name via LatheAxis::chord_in_meridian\n  (out-of-plane offset vs MERIDIAN_TOL); simulate_lathe_about checks\n  every straight chord up front so a refusal writes nothing. Parting\n  through and past centre still cuts.\n- lathe_field_sim: the off-origin bar's setup puts G54 on its axis\n  (3, -2), so the machine spindle IS the fitted axis (#62 guarantees\n  this at generation); the module laws say the field revolves about\n  the fitted axis, which is the spindle.\n- stock_lathe: a leaned-axis (10 deg) parity case pins the general\n  window reach and the leaned meridian split; skewed-chord refusal and\n  past-centre parting cases.\n- stock_sim_lathe laws: the nose circle is the whole modelled solid\n  (no flank/holder sweep, unlike the mill shank); a milling tool on a\n  turning op gets its own refusal text, not the column engine's.\n\nRefs #19\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
